# =============================================================================
# mtg-assistant: local configuration
# =============================================================================
# This file (.env.example) is committed and documents every setting.
# Copy it to .env (which Git ignores) and fill in the values there:
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# mise loads .env into every `mise run ...` task, so the gh and wrangler CLIs
# pick these up automatically, with no interactive login. `mise run setup:accounts`
# then pushes the right values to Cloudflare (Worker secrets) and GitHub
# (Actions secrets).
#
# Never paste these values into a chat, an issue or a commit. If a value
# leaks, revoke it at its source and make a new one.
#
# Suggested order (some steps depend on earlier ones):
#   1. Cloudflare account and zone IDs
#   2. Cloudflare Zero Trust team domain (the Access Google client needs it)
#   3. Google Cloud project, consent screen and both OAuth clients
#   4. The three Cloudflare API tokens
#   5. GitHub token
#   6. Allowlist
# =============================================================================


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Cloudflare account and zone
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Your Cloudflare account ID (not secret, but kept here so it's in one place).
# Where to find it: dash.cloudflare.com → Workers & Pages → Overview, under
# "Account details" in the right sidebar. It's also the long hex string in the
# dashboard URL: dash.cloudflare.com/<ACCOUNT_ID>/...
CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=

# Zone ID for conrad.tools.
# Where to find it: dash.cloudflare.com → conrad.tools → Overview, under "API"
# in the right sidebar → Zone ID.
CLOUDFLARE_ZONE_ID=

# The hostname the server is served from. setup:accounts and wrangler.jsonc use it.
MTG_ASSISTANT_HOST=mtg-assistant.conrad.tools


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. Cloudflare Zero Trust (Access): the login wall in front of the browser pages
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Access guards /authorize, /callback, /upload and /download. The free plan covers
# up to 50 users. Cloudflare may ask for a card on file, even for the $0 plan.
#
# How to set it up:
#   1. Go to dash.cloudflare.com → Zero Trust. On first visit, pick a team name
#      (for example "conrad") and the Free plan.
#   2. Your team domain is <team>.cloudflareaccess.com. You'll also find it under
#      Zero Trust → Settings → Custom Pages (or Team domain).
#   3. Leave the identity provider for now. setup:accounts adds the Google login
#      once the values in section 3 are filled in.

# Example: conrad.cloudflareaccess.com (no https://)
CLOUDFLARE_ACCESS_TEAM_DOMAIN=


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. Google OAuth: a free personal Google account is all you need
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# You need two OAuth clients in one Google Cloud project: one for the app's own
# login, and one for the Cloudflare Access login.
#
# Project and consent screen (one-time setup):
#   1. Go to console.cloud.google.com, then project picker → New project. Name it
#      "mtg-assistant". You don't need to turn on billing.
#   2. Go to APIs & Services → OAuth consent screen (also called "Google Auth Platform").
#        - User type: External
#        - App name: MTG Assistant. Support and developer email: yours.
#        - Scopes: only openid, .../auth/userinfo.email and .../auth/userinfo.profile.
#          These are non-sensitive, so Google won't ask to verify the app.
#        - Publishing status: leave it on "Testing".
#        - Test users (under Audience): add your Gmail. Add Brad only when you
#          decide to invite him. In Testing mode, only listed test users can
#          sign in, so this works as an extra allowlist.
#
# Client A, the app's login (used by the MCP server's OAuth flow):
#   APIs & Services → Credentials → Create credentials → OAuth client ID
#     - Application type: Web application
#     - Name: mtg-assistant app
#     - Authorized redirect URIs:
#         https://mtg-assistant.conrad.tools/callback
#         http://localhost:8787/callback        (local `wrangler dev`)
#     - Copy the Client ID and Client secret into the two lines below.
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=

# Client B, the Cloudflare Access login (it needs the team domain from section 2):
#   APIs & Services → Credentials → Create credentials → OAuth client ID
#     - Application type: Web application
#     - Name: mtg-assistant cloudflare access
#     - Authorized JavaScript origins:
#         https://<team>.cloudflareaccess.com
#     - Authorized redirect URIs:
#         https://<team>.cloudflareaccess.com/cdn-cgi/access/callback
#     - Copy the Client ID and Client secret into the two lines below.
# If you'd rather not create Client B, leave these empty. setup:accounts then
# uses Access's built-in "One-time PIN" login, which emails a code to allowlisted
# addresses.
ACCESS_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
ACCESS_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4. Cloudflare API tokens: three tokens, each with least privilege
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Create each one at dash.cloudflare.com → My Profile → API Tokens → Create Token
# → "Create Custom Token". For every token:
#   - Account Resources: Include → your account only
#   - Zone Resources (where zone permissions apply): Include → Specific zone → conrad.tools
#   - TTL: an end date about 90 days out. `mise run secrets:check` warns before expiry.
#   - Client IP Address Filtering (optional, admin token only): your home IP. Skip
#     this if your IP changes often.
# The permission names below match Cloudflare's dropdowns. If a name has moved,
# pick the nearest match. The first `setup:accounts` run reports any permission
# it's missing.

# 4a. ADMIN token, used only locally by `mise run setup:accounts` and the
# auth/audit tasks. It creates infrastructure, so it never leaves this machine.
#   Account permissions:
#     - Workers Scripts: Edit
#     - D1: Edit
#     - Workers R2 Storage: Edit
#     - Workers KV Storage: Edit
#     - Access: Apps and Policies: Edit
#     - Access: Organizations, Identity Providers, and Groups: Edit
#     - Notifications: Edit
#     - Account Settings: Read
#   Zone permissions (conrad.tools only):
#     - Zone: Read
#     - DNS: Edit
#     - Workers Routes: Edit
#     - Zone WAF: Edit          (custom rules and rate limiting rules)
#     - Zone Settings: Edit     (Always Use HTTPS, HSTS, Bot Fight Mode)
#     - Config Rules: Edit
CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=

# 4b. DEPLOY token. setup:accounts stores it in the GitHub "production" environment,
# and only deploy.yml uses it.
#   Account permissions:
#     - Workers Scripts: Edit   (deploy and rollback)
#     - D1: Edit                (apply migrations)
#     - Workers KV Storage: Read
#     - Account Settings: Read
#   Zone permissions (conrad.tools only):
#     - Zone: Read
#     - Workers Routes: Edit
#     - DNS: Edit               (the Worker custom domain record)
CLOUDFLARE_DEPLOY_API_TOKEN=

# 4c. INGEST token. setup:accounts stores it in GitHub for the nightly Scryfall job.
#   Account permissions:
#     - D1: Edit
#   (no zone permissions)
CLOUDFLARE_INGEST_API_TOKEN=


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 5. GitHub: a fine-grained personal access token for this one repo
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# gh reads GH_TOKEN, and setup:accounts uses it to set Actions secrets, create the
# "production" environment and add the main-branch ruleset.
#
# How to create it:
#   github.com → Settings → Developer settings → Personal access tokens →
#   Fine-grained tokens → Generate new token
#     - Token name: mtg-assistant setup
#     - Expiration: 90 days
#     - Resource owner: danielmconrad
#     - Repository access: Only select repositories → danielmconrad/mtg-assistant
#     - Repository permissions:
#         Actions: Read and write
#         Administration: Read and write   (rulesets and environments)
#         Contents: Read and write
#         Environments: Read and write
#         Secrets: Read and write
#         Workflows: Read and write
#         Metadata: Read-only              (required, selected automatically)
GH_TOKEN=


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 6. Access control
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The emails allowed to sign in, comma-separated and lowercase, with no spaces.
# The server, the Cloudflare Access policy and the Google test-user list each
# check sign-ins independently. setup:accounts keeps the first two in sync, and
# Google's test users are maintained by hand (section 3). To invite Brad later,
# add his email here, add him as a Google test user, then run
# `mise run setup:accounts`.
ALLOWED_EMAILS=

# Optional: your home IP. It's used for the optional /mcp IP pinning (so Claude
# Code on this machine still gets through) and for the admin token's IP filter.
# Leave it empty to turn both off.
ADMIN_HOME_IP=


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated automatically: don't add these here
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# setup:accounts generates DOWNLOAD_SIGNING_KEY and UPLOAD_SIGNING_KEY (32 random
# bytes each) and the OAuth provider's KV encryption material, then stores them
# directly as Worker secrets. They're never written to disk or shown.
